/-! # Totally ramified base change of a weakly unramified DVR extension

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tag 09ER,
`lemma-weakly-unramified-goes-up-along-totally-ramified`, with complete base DVRs.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-epp-totally-ramified-base-change)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w x y

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace IsDiscreteValuationRing

/-- Totally ramified finite separable base change preserves a weakly unramified extension
of complete DVRs. Both residue-field isomorphisms commute with the structural maps;
the normalization isomorphism is specified on every pure tensor. The local structure on
`integralClosure A K₁` makes the maximal ideal in the total ramification hypotheses explicit.

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tag 09ER,
`lemma-weakly-unramified-goes-up-along-totally-ramified`.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-epp-totally-ramified-base-change)

Proof:
1. A is a PID, hence Noetherian and normal (lem-weil-pbc-pid-noetherian-normal), and
   complete local, hence Nagata (lem-weil-pbc-complete-local-nagata). The definitions of
   Nagata and Japanese rings give finiteness of A₁ over A. The integral-closure fraction-field
   lemma and the domain case of lem-weil-pbc-finite-over-complete-local-product make A₁
   a complete local domain with fraction field K₁. By lem-sc-dvr-dimension-one and
   lem-sfb-finite-normalization-local-dvr, its localization at the maximal ideal is a DVR;
   as A₁ is local, this is A₁ itself. The totally ramified uniformizer presentation
   (lem-sfb-totally-ramified-uniformizer-presentation) writes A₁ = A[T]/(P), with P monic
   Eisenstein of degree [K₁:K].
2. The maximal-ideal equality for A → B makes a uniformizer of A a uniformizer of B.
   The polynomial remains Eisenstein over B. By lem-sfb-eisenstein-quotient-dvr,
   C = B[T]/(P) is a DVR, with maximal ideal generated by the class of T.
3. The polynomial presentations identify B ⊗[A] A₁ with C and L ⊗[K] K₁ with C[1/π].
   The unit-times-uniformizer-power lemma identifies B[1/π] with L. The monic quotient
   is free of rank [K₁:K] (lem-weil-pbc-monic-quotient-free). Thus C[1/π] is a nonzero
   finite-dimensional domain over L, hence a field (lem-weil-pbc-finite-dimensional-domain-
   is-field), and it is the fraction field of C.
4. Modulo T, the quotient is B/(π), compatibly with constants, giving the residue-field
   isomorphism. Finiteness over complete B and the domain case of the finite-over-complete-
   local-product theorem give completeness of C. It is integral over B and normal since it
   is a DVR. Every element of its fraction field integral over B is integral over C, hence
   belongs to C: C is the integral closure. The two polynomial presentations send b ⊗ a
   to the indicated pure tensor in L ⊗[K] K₁. Finally the uniformizer of A₁ maps to T, so
   its maximal ideal extends to the maximal ideal of C.
-/
theorem totally_ramified_base_change
    (A : Type u) (B : Type v) (K : Type w) (L : Type x) (K₁ : Type y)
    [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsDiscreteValuationRing A]
    [CommRing B] [IsDomain B] [IsDiscreteValuationRing B]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B) B]
    [Field K] [Field L] [Field K₁]
    [Algebra A B] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)]
    [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K]
    [Algebra B L] [IsFractionRing B L]
    [Algebra K L] [Algebra A L] [IsScalarTower A K L] [IsScalarTower A B L]
    [Algebra K K₁] [Algebra A K₁] [IsScalarTower A K K₁]
    [FiniteDimensional K K₁] [Algebra.IsSeparable K K₁]
    [IsLocalRing (integralClosure A K₁)]
    (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B))
    (hweak : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A B) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)
    (hres : ∃ e : IsLocalRing.ResidueField A ≃+*
      IsLocalRing.ResidueField (integralClosure A K₁),
      ∀ a : A, e (IsLocalRing.residue A a) =
        IsLocalRing.residue (integralClosure A K₁) (algebraMap A (integralClosure A K₁) a))
    (hram : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A (integralClosure A K₁)) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (integralClosure A K₁) ^ Module.finrank K K₁) :
    IsField (L ⊗[K] K₁) ∧
      (∃ e : (B ⊗[A] integralClosure A K₁) ≃ₐ[B] integralClosure B (L ⊗[K] K₁),
        ∀ (b : B) (a : integralClosure A K₁),
          (e (b ⊗ₜ[A] a) : L ⊗[K] K₁) = algebraMap B L b ⊗ₜ[K] (a : K₁)) ∧
      ∃ (hC : IsDomain (B ⊗[A] integralClosure A K₁))
        (hDVR : IsDiscreteValuationRing (B ⊗[A] integralClosure A K₁)),
        IsAdicComplete
          (@IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (B ⊗[A] integralClosure A K₁) _ hDVR.toIsLocalRing)
          (B ⊗[A] integralClosure A K₁) ∧
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (integralClosure A K₁)).map
          Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight.toRingHom =
            @IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (B ⊗[A] integralClosure A K₁) _ hDVR.toIsLocalRing ∧
        ∃ e : IsLocalRing.ResidueField B ≃+*
          @IsLocalRing.ResidueField (B ⊗[A] integralClosure A K₁) _ hDVR.toIsLocalRing,
          ∀ b : B, e (IsLocalRing.residue B b) =
            @IsLocalRing.residue (B ⊗[A] integralClosure A K₁) _ hDVR.toIsLocalRing
              (algebraMap B (B ⊗[A] integralClosure A K₁) b) := by
  sorry

end IsDiscreteValuationRing
